  <p class="eyebrow">Guide</p>
  <h1>Quick start</h1>
  <p class="lede">About fifteen minutes to a budget you can spend from. ZxBudget has no account of its own. You can stop after any step and come back.</p>

  <h2>1. Open the app</h2>
  <p>Open ZxBudget on your iPhone, iPad, or Mac. To use the same budget on your other Apple devices, sign into iCloud on each one (the iPhone Settings app, or System Settings on a Mac). One device works without that.</p>

  <h2>2. Create your budget</h2>
  <p>The first screen says <strong>Welcome to ZxBudget</strong>.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Choose <strong>Create my budget</strong>. If someone is inviting you instead, choose <strong>I'm joining a shared budget</strong> and accept their invite. Nothing is created on this device until the shared budget arrives.</li>
    <li>On <strong>Your Budget</strong>, set the name and the base currency. Canadian dollars is already selected. Tap <strong>Next</strong>.</li>
    <li>On <strong>How detailed?</strong>, pick a starting structure: Simple, Balanced, Detailed, or Blank. Balanced is the one selected to start. Tap <strong>Create</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>You can rename, add, or delete categories later. The template is only a starting point.</p>

  <h2>3. Set your account balances</h2>
  <p>A new budget includes two accounts, <strong>Chequing</strong> and <strong>Credit Card</strong>, both at zero. Each has an Opening Balance transaction.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Open the account and edit that Opening Balance so the amount and date match what the account holds today.</li>
    <li>Or delete the placeholder and use <strong>Add Account</strong>. A new account asks for <strong>Balance</strong> and <strong>As of</strong>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Add savings, cash, or another card the same way. The accounts you spend from are enough to begin.</p>

  <h2>4. Record income</h2>
  <p>On iPhone, tap the <strong>+</strong> in the tab bar. On Mac, use <strong>Add Transaction</strong> or press ⌘N.</p>
  <p>Switch the amount to <strong>Inflow</strong>. The category starts at <strong>Ready to Assign</strong>. Enter the pay and the account it landed in, then save. That money waits in Ready to Assign until you give it a category.</p>

  <h2>5. Assign the month</h2>
  <p>Open the <strong>Budget</strong> tab. Ready to Assign is at the top.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>On Mac, click a category’s <strong>Assigned</strong> amount and type what this month needs.</li>
    <li>On iPhone, tap the category and edit <strong>Assigned</strong>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Stop when Ready to Assign is zero, or leave some of it there on purpose. Unassigned money stays visible.</p>

  <h2>6. Record spending</h2>
  <p>Add another transaction and leave it on <strong>Outflow</strong>. Pick the category you spent from and save. That category’s available amount drops by what you spent.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <p>Want to click around before entering your own numbers? Open <strong>Try Demo Mode</strong> in Settings. On iPhone, Settings is in the <strong>···</strong> menu. On Mac, it is in the ZxBudget menu (⌘,). <strong>Exit Demo</strong> on the banner is the way back. The sample budget never mixes with yours.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>When something looks wrong</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:zxiiro@gmail.com?subject=ZxBudget%20Support">zxiiro@gmail.com</a> with your device model and OS version. For where data lives, read the <a href="/privacy.html">privacy policy</a>.</p>
